<section class="dit-home-section" aria-labelledby="dit-home-workflow-title">
	<div class="dit-home-section-heading">
		<h2 id="dit-home-workflow-title">Review data like code</h2>
		<p>dit turns dataset work into traceable repository workflows: clone data, inspect rows, propose changes, review diffs, and merge with governance.</p>
	</div>
	<div class="dit-home-feature-grid">
		<a class="dit-home-feature" href="{{AppSubUrl}}/explore/repos">
			{{svg "octicon-repo" 26}}
			<strong>Dataset repositories</strong>
			<span>Browse public datasets, commits, branches, and row previews.</span>
		</a>
		<a class="dit-home-feature" href="{{AppSubUrl}}/pulls">
			{{svg "octicon-git-pull-request" 26}}
			<strong>Review queues</strong>
			<span>Follow dataset pull requests from proposed rows to accepted changes.</span>
		</a>
		<a class="dit-home-feature" href="{{AppSubUrl}}/repo/create">
			{{svg "octicon-plus" 26}}
			<strong>Create a data repo</strong>
			<span>Start a governed dataset workspace backed by Git storage.</span>
		</a>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="dit-home-section dit-home-steps" aria-labelledby="dit-home-steps-title">
	<div class="dit-home-section-heading">
		<h2 id="dit-home-steps-title">A short path from data to review</h2>
	</div>
	<ol>
		<li>
			<strong>Authenticate</strong>
			<span>Sign in, create a token, and connect dit clients or scripts.</span>
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Prepare changes</strong>
			<span>Clone a dataset repo, edit JSONL or other managed assets, and push a branch.</span>
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Inspect and merge</strong>
			<span>Use DataHub Gateway to preview rows, discuss diffs, and merge reviewed updates.</span>
		</li>
	</ol>
</section>
